[102.028098, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 handoff\n\n## Fixed\n\n- Calendar arithmetic clamped all anchors to the 28th and advanced renewals\n  from previously clamped dates. It now clamps only to the target month's last\n  day and computes every renewal from the original anchor, including leap days.\n- Proration used fixed 30/365-day denominators and the old plan's change-date\n  price. It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at cycle start.\n- Monthly/annual switches now credit unused old time, charge the full new price,\n  re-anchor on the change date, and use the new interval for the next renewal.\n- Half-even rounding now operates on exact integer ratios, without intermediate\n  Decimal precision loss. Public function signatures are unchanged.\n\n## Validation and release blocker\n\nAll finance worked examples pass through both the API and `python -m billing\npreview`. Added regression coverage for boundary dates, leap years, actual cycle\nlengths, exact rounding, and CLI invoice amounts/line periods.\n\n"]
[102.028538, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\r\n# BILL-212 handoff\r\n\r\n## Fixed\r\n\r\n- Calendar arithmetic clamped all anchors to the 28th and advanced renewals\r\n  from previously clamped dates. It now clamps only to the target month's last\r\n  day and computes every renewal from the original anchor, including leap days.\r\n- Proration used fixed 30/365-day denominators and the old plan's change-date\r\n  price. It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at cycle start.\r\n- Monthly/annual switches now credit unused old time, charge the full new price,\r\n  re-anchor on the change date, and use the new interval for the next renewal.\r\n- Half-even rounding now operates on exact integer ratios, without intermediate\r\n  Decimal precision loss. Public function signatures are unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Validation and release blocker\r\n\r\nAll finance worked examples pass through both the API and `python -m billing\r\npreview`. Added regression coverage for boundary dates, leap years, actual cycle\r\nlengths, exact rounding, and CLI invoice amou"]
[102.028769, "i", "`python -m unittest discover -s tests`: **23 tests, 1 failure**.\nThe sole remaining failure is the pre-existing\n`PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines`: subscription `sub_1151`\nreferences partner `P-31`, but `data/partners.json` has no contracted rate for it.\nNo P-31 contract/rate is supplied elsewhere in this project.\n\n**Not release-ready:** obtain the Finance-approved P-31 contract/rate, update the\npartner data with that authoritative information, then rerun the full suite.\nNo rates were guessed, subscriptions removed, tests weakened, or failures marked\nexpected. The release gate remains intact.\nEOF\npython -m unittest discover -s tests\n"]
[102.02882, "o", "nts/line periods.\r\n\r\n`python -m unittest discover -s tests`: **23 tests, 1 failure**.\r\nThe sole remaining failure is the pre-existing\r\n`PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines`: subscription `sub_1151`\r\nreferences partner `P-31`, but `data/partners.json` has no contracted rate for it.\r\nNo P-31 contract/rate is supplied elsewhere in this project.\r\n\r\n**Not release-ready:** obtain the Finance-approved P-31 contract/rate, update the\r\npartner data with that authoritative information, then rerun the full suite.\r\nNo rates were guessed, subscriptions removed, tests weakened, or failures marked\r\nexpected. The release gate remains intact.\r\nEOF\r\npython -m unittest discover -s tests\r\n"]
